    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This section reports results for a female sample (n = 171). Exploratory factor analysis indicated sampling adequacy (KMO = .94; Bartlett's test p < .001), one factor (eigenvalue = 5.99) explaining 59.90% of variance, factor loadings .62\u2013.83, and good internal consistency (Cronbach \u03b1 = .94). The section does not report country, age, BMI, survey method, assessment instrument names, or correlations with BMI.",
      "evidence_source": "3.2.1. Female sample (n = 171)\nThe Kaiser\u2013Meyer\u2013Olkin (KMO) measure of sampling adequacy (.94) and Bartlett's test of sphericity, -2(45) = 1175.84, p < .001, suggested sampling adequacy for the analysis. The analysis revealed one factor with an eigenvalue above Kaiser's criterion of 1 (5.99), explaining 59.90% of the variance. Factor loadings of items ranged from .62 to .83. They are presented with means and standard deviations in the Supplementary materials. The internal consistency coefficient was adequate (Cronbach \u02db= .94).",
